        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Hustlenomics, Excuse My French, Pop That\n- Companies: Bad Boy Records, Coke Boys Records, Maybach Music Group, Interscope Records\n- People: Gorilla Zoe, Rick Ross, Drake, Lil Wayne\n- Concepts: record labels, singles\n\nFacts:\n- Hustlenomics was released by Bad Boy Records on August 28, 2007.\n- Hustlenomics contains the singles Coffee Shop and Bottle Poppin, and both songs feature Gorilla Zoe.\n- Bad Boy Entertainment, also known as Bad Boy Records, is an American record label.\n- Excuse My French was released on May 21, 2013, by Coke Boys Records, Bad Boy Records, Maybach Music Group, and Interscope Records.\n- Pop That was released as the first single from the 2013 debut studio album Excuse My French.\n- Pop That features guest appearances from Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.",
